@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Bluetooth USB Drivers
+
+This system extension provides the Linux Bluetooth core, USB HCI, and vendor
+helper kernel modules built for the matching Talos kernel. The rfkill subsystem
+is built into the matching kernel. Validated hardware includes Realtek
+`0bda:b85b` and MediaTek `0e8d:7922` controllers.
+
+The extension does not include firmware, BlueZ, or D-Bus. Select a matching
+firmware extension for the controller: official `siderolabs/realtek-firmware`
+for Realtek or `mediatek-bluetooth-firmware` for the validated MT7922 device.
+Bluetooth userspace belongs in a separate extension or workload.
+
+## Installation
+
+Select `siderolabs/bluetooth-usb-drivers` and the required firmware extension
+when creating the Talos boot asset or installer.
+See [Installing Extensions](https://github.com/siderolabs/extensions#installing-extensions).
+
+Load the USB HCI driver through the machine configuration:
+
+```yaml
+machine:
+  kernel:
+    modules:
+      - name: btusb
+```
+
+Kernel module dependencies load `bluetooth`, `btintel`, and `btrtl` as needed.
+
+## Verification
+
+Confirm that the modules loaded without kernel errors:
+
+```console
+talosctl -n <IP> read /proc/modules
+talosctl -n <IP> dmesg
+```
+
+Confirm that the kernel created an HCI device:
+
+```console
+talosctl -n <IP> ls /sys/class/bluetooth
+```
+
+An `hci0` device proves only the kernel layer. Applications such as Home
+Assistant additionally require a compatible BlueZ daemon and its system D-Bus
+API; those userspace components are outside this extension.
